From 1782af32c894dc514aafe0f8bda4dd6f43778156 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 19:20:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 146/210] arm64: dts: meson: gx: carry HDMI audio from the
 SPDIF encoder

The AIU IEC958 encoder only feeds the optical output on boards that have
one, so a compressed stream cannot be sent over HDMI. Link the encoder to
the HDMI controller on all GX boards, adding the S/PDIF FIFO and encoder
links to boards without an optical output.

hdmi_tx now has an I2S and an S/PDIF DAI, so name the I2S DAI in the
existing HDMI link of the HiFi-Shield boards, which do not use the
common sound card layout.

Place the S/PDIF FIFO link second on every board so the PCM device that
carries compressed audio has the same number across the family.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
